node_modules/
/dist/
/coverage/
# Working documents under docs/ are agent and author scratch space - plans,
# specs, reports, runbooks, follow-up registers. They are deliberately not part
# of the repository, so the default here is deny.
#
# Ignoring `/docs/*` rather than `/docs/` matters: git does not descend into an
# ignored directory, so a negation inside one can never take effect. Ignoring
# the entries under docs/ instead leaves the directory itself walkable, which is
# what makes the opt-in below work.
#
# To track a directory under docs/, add a negation next to the one below. Only
# durable, repository-owned reference material belongs there - anything a reader
# with a clone alone must be able to resolve.
/docs/*
!/docs/reference/
/external/
.claude/settings.local.json
/.agents/
/.claude/skills/
/skills-lock.json
